Madam,

You have risen very high, and I am glad of it. I ask only a small place at co=
urt, in memory of the friendship we shared before your marriage.

I am sure neither of us wishes old letters and older promises to be the talk =
of the household. A secretaryship would settle the matter handsomely.

Your old friend,
Francis Dereham
